# ============================================================
# How it works
# ============================================================
#
# When a PR modifies /proxy/main.go:
#   1. GitHub reads CODEOWNERS.
#   2. It finds the last matching pattern for the path.
#   3. It assigns @gasciljh as a reviewer automatically.
#
# When a PR modifies /proxy/install_app.sh (CO-V15-01):
#   → matched by /proxy/ and /proxy/install_app.sh.
#   → Reviewer MUST verify:
#       • 5 cascade levels intact
#       • 75-second deadline present
#       • Three-way trap split (EXIT/INT/TERM)
#       • SELinux staging still uses /data/local/tmp/
#       • No `setenforce 0`
#       • Play Protect trap restores `$_VERIFIER_ORIG`
#     See docs/SECURITY.md §5.36 and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5.8.
#
# When a PR modifies /proxy/boot-mini.sh (CO-V15-01):
#   → matched by /proxy/ and /proxy/boot-mini.sh.
#   → Reviewer MUST verify:
#       • The file still defines all 5 primitives + _MONITORING_UI_PORT
#       • functions.sh still sources it (no redefinition)
#       → CI Step 9 in ci.yml will catch regressions automatically.
#
# When a PR modifies /proxy/go.mod or /proxy/go.sum (CO-V15-01):
#   → A new external dependency requires its own ADR (ADR-0002
#     compliance rule).
#
# When a PR modifies /docs/MANIFEST_NOTES.md (CO-V15-03):
#   → Reviewer MUST verify that every `x-note-*` field extracted
#     from web/manifest.json is still documented here.
#
# When a PR modifies /.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml (CO-V15-03):
#   → Reviewer MUST verify that any new `exclude:` block has a
#     documented rationale and that no `go/path-injection` or
#     `go/command-injection` rule is suppressed.
#
# ============================================================
# Benefits
# ============================================================
#
# ✅ Faster review: the reviewer is assigned immediately.
# ✅ No oversight: every PR is automatically reviewed.
# ✅ Fine-grained: each file can have a different reviewer.
# ✅ Team-friendly: supports team handles.
# ✅ ADR-aware: architectural decisions trigger the right reviewer.
# ✅ Data-preservation-aware (v1.2.0).
